or window. Reload to refresh your session. You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session. Dismiss alert\nL114: \nL115: cite61†zai-org / cite62†GLM-OCR Public\nL116: \nL117:   * cite63†Notifications You must be signed in to change notification settings\nL118:   * cite63†Fork 670 L119:   * cite63†Star L120:   * cite62†Code L121:   * cite64†Issues 40 L122:   * cite65†Pull requests 20 L123:   * cite66†Actions L124:   * cite67†Projects L125:   * cite68†Security and quality 0 L126:   * cite69†Insights L127: \nL128: Additional navigation options\nL129: \nL130: main\nL131: \nL132: cite70†Branches cite71†Tags L133: \nL134: [Input: Go to file]\nL135: \nL136: Go to file\nL137: \nL138: Code\nL139: \nL140: Open more actions menu\nL141: ## Latest commit\nL142: \nL143: \nL144: \nL145: ## History\nL146: \nL147: 110 Commits\nL148: ## Folders and files\nL149: Name  | Name  | Last commit message  | Last commit date\nL150: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL151: cite72†.github | cite72†.github |    |\nL152: cite73†apps | cite73†apps |    |\nL153: cite74†examples | cite74†examples |    |\nL154: cite75†glmocr | cite75†glmocr |    |\nL155: cite76†resources | cite76†resources |    |\nL156: cite77†skills | cite77†skills |    |\nL157: cite78†.gitignore | cite78†.gitignore |    |\nL158: cite79†.pre-commit-config.yaml | cite79†.pre-commit-config.yaml |    |\nL159: cite80†LICENSE | cite80†LICENSE |    |\nL160: cite81†README.md | cite81†README.md |    |\nL161: cite82†README_zh.md | cite82†README_zh.md |    |\nL162: cite83†agent.md | cite83†agent.md |    |\nL163: cite84†pyproject.toml | cite84†pyproject.toml |    |\nL164: [Button: View all files]\nL165: ## Repository files navigation\nL166: \nL167:   *   * cite85†README L168:   * cite85†Apache-2.0 license L169: \nL170: More items\nL171: \nL172: ## GLM-OCR\nL173: \nL174: cite82†中文阅读 L175: \nL176: 👋 Join our cite86†WeChat and cite87†Discord†discord.gg community\nL177: 📖 Check out the GLM-OCR cite88†technical report†arxiv.org L178: 📍 Use GLM-OCR's cite89†API†docs.z.ai L179: ### Model Introduction\nL180: GLM-OCR is a multimodal OCR model for complex document understanding, built on the GLM-V encoder–decoder architecture. It introduces Multi-Token Prediction (MTP) loss and stable full-task reinforcement learning to improve training efficiency, recognition accuracy, and generalization. The model integrates the CogViT visual encoder pre-trained on large-scale image–text data, a lightweight cross-modal connector with efficient token downsampling, and a GLM-0.5B language decoder.\nL181: Combined with a two-stage pipeline of layout analysis and parallel recognition based on PP-DocLayout-V3, GLM-OCR delivers robust and high-quality OCR performance across diverse document layouts.\nL182: Key Features\nL183: \nL184:   * State-of-the-Art Performance: Achieves a score of 94.62 on OmniDocBench V1.5, ranking #1 overall, and delivers state-of-the-art results across major document understanding benchmarks, including formula recognition, table recognition, and information extraction.\nL185: \nL186:   * Optimized for Real-World Scenarios: Designed and optimized for practical business use cases, maintaining robust performance on complex tables, code-heavy documents, seals, and other challenging real-world layouts.\nL187:   * Efficient Inference: With only 0.9B parameters, GLM-OCR supports deployment via vLLM, SGLang, and Ollama, significantly reducing inference latency and compute cost, making it ideal for high-concurrency services and edge deployments.\nL188: \nL189:   * Easy to Use: Fully open-sourced and equipped with a comprehensive cite62†SDK and inference toolchain, offering simple installation, one-line invocation, and smooth integration into existing production pipelines.\nL190: ### News & Updates\nL191: \nL192:   * [2026.3.12] GLM-OCR SDK now supports agent-friendly Skill mode — just `pip install glmocr` + set API key, ready to use via CLI or Python with no GPU or YAML config needed. See: cite90†GLM-OCR Skill L193:   * [2026.3.12] GLM-OCR Technical Report is now available. See: cite88†GLM-OCR Technical Report†arxiv.org L194:   * [2026.2.12] Fine-tuning tutorial based on LLaMA-Factory is now available. See: cite91†GLM-OCR Fine-tuning Guide L195: ### Download Model\nL196: \nL197: Model  | Download Links  | Precision\nL198: --- | --- | ---\nL199: GLM-OCR  | cite92†🤗 Hugging Face†huggingface.co L200: cite93†🤖 ModelScope†modelscope.cn | BF16\nL201: \nL202: ## GLM-OCR SDK\nL203: \nL204: We provide an SDK for using GLM-OCR more efficiently and conveniently.\nL205: ### Install SDK\nL206: \nL207: Choose the lightest installation that matches your scenario:\nL208: \nL209:     # Cloud / MaaS + local images / PDFs (fastest install)\nL210:     pip install glmocr\nL211: \nL212:     # Self-hosted pipeline (layout detection)\nL213:     pip install \"glmocr[selfhosted]\"\nL214: \nL215:     # Flask service support\nL216:     pip install \"glmocr[server]\"\nL217: Install from source for development:\nL218: \nL219:     # Install from source\nL220:     git clone https://github.com/zai-org/glm-ocr.git\nL221:     cd glm-ocr\nL222:     uv venv --python 3.12 --seed && source .venv/bin/activate\nL223:     uv pip install -e .\nL224: ### Model Deployment\nL225: \nL226: Two ways to use GLM-OCR:\nL227: #### Option 1: Zhipu MaaS API (Recommended for Quick Start)\nL228: \nL229: Use the hosted cloud API – no GPU needed. The cloud service runs the complete GLM-OCR pipeline internally, so the SDK simply forwards your request and returns the result.\nL230: \nL231:   1. Get an API key from cite94†https://open.bigmodel.cn†open.bigmodel.cn L232:   2. Configure `config.yaml`:\nL233: \nL234:     pipeline:\nL235:       maas:\nL236:         enabled: true # Enable MaaS mode\nL237:         api_key: your-api-key # Required\nL238: That's it! When `maas.enabled=true`, the SDK acts as a thin wrapper that:\nL239: \nL240:   * Forwards your documents to the Zhipu cloud API\nL241:   * Returns the results directly (Markdown + JSON layout details)\nL242:   * No local processing, no GPU required\nL243: Input note (MaaS): the upstream API accepts `file` as a URL or a `data:<mime>;base64,...` data URI. If you have raw base64 without the `data:` prefix, wrap it as a data URI (recommended). The SDK will auto-wrap local file paths / bytes / raw base64 into a data URI when calling MaaS.\nL244: \nL245: API documentation: cite95†https://docs.bigmodel.cn/cn/guide/models/vlm/glm-ocr†docs.bigmodel.cn L246: #### Option 2: Self-host with vLLM / SGLang\nL247: \nL248: Deploy the GLM-OCR model locally for full control. The SDK provides the complete pipeline: layout detection, parallel region OCR, and result formatting.\nL249: \nL250: Install the self-hosted extra first:\nL251: \nL252:     pip install \"glmocr[selfhosted]\"\nL253: ##### Using vLLM\nL254: \nL255: Install vLLM:\nL256: \nL257:     docker pull vllm/vllm-openai:v0.19.0-ubuntu2404\nL258: \nL259: Or using with pip:\nL260: \nL261:     pip install -U \"vllm>=0.19.0\"\nL262: \nL263: Launch the service:\nL264: \nL265:     pip install \"transformers>=5.3.0\"\nL266: \nL267:     vllm serve zai-org/GLM-OCR  --port 8080 --speculative-config '{\"method\": \"mtp\", \"num_speculative_tokens\": 3}' --served-model-name glm-ocr\nL268: \nL269: > Note Add `--max-model-len` and `--gpu-memory-utilization` according to Your own machine to handle large image/pdf\nL270: ##### Using SGLang\nL271: \nL272: Install SGLang:\nL273: \nL274:     docker pull lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.10\nL275: \nL276: Or using with pip:\nL277: \nL278:     pip install \"sglang>=0.5.10\"\nL279: \nL280: Launch the service:\nL281: \nL282:     SGLANG_ENABLE_SPEC_V2=1 sglang serve --model-path zai-org/GLM-OCR --port 8080 --speculative-algorithm NEXTN --speculative-num-steps 3 --speculative-eagle-topk 1 --speculative-num-draft-tokens 4 --served-model-name glm-ocr\nL283: \nL284: > Note Add `--context-len` and `--mem-fraction-static` according to Your own machine to handle large image/pdf\nL285: #### Option 3: Ollama/MLX\nL286: \nL287: For specialized deployment scenarios, see the detailed guides:\nL288: \nL289:   * cite96†Apple Silicon with mlx-vlm - Optimized for Apple Silicon Macs\nL290:   * cite97†Ollama Deployment - Simple local deployment with Ollama\nL291: #### Option 4: SDK Server + Client (GPU-less Client)\nL292: \nL293: Deploy the SDK Server on a GPU machine, then use any machine as a client — no GPU needed on the client side. The client connects via the MaaS-compatible protocol, pointing `api_url` at your self-hosted server.\nL294: \nL295:     # Client config.yaml\nL296:     pipeline:\nL297:       maas:\nL298:         enabled: true\nL299:         api_url: http://<SERVER_IP>:5002/glmocr/parse\nL300:         api_key: any-string    # self-hosted server does not validate keys\nL301:         verify_ssl: false\nL302: See the full guide: cite98†Self-hosted SDK Server + Client L303: #### Update Configuration\nL304: \nL305: After launching the service, configure `config.yaml`:\nL306: \nL307:     pipeline:\nL308:       maas:\nL309:         enabled: false # Disable MaaS mode (default)\nL310:       ocr_api:\nL311:         api_host: localhost # or your vLLM/SGLang server address\nL312:         api_port: 8080\nL313: \nL314: ### SDK Usage Guide\nL315: #### CLI\nL316: \nL317:     # Parse a single image\nL318:     glmocr parse examples/source/code.png\nL319: \nL320:     # Parse a directory\nL321:     glmocr parse examples/source/\nL322: \nL323:     # Set output directory\nL324:     glmocr parse examples/source/code.png --output ./results/\nL325: \nL326:     # Use a custom config\nL327:     glmocr parse examples/source/code.png --config my_config.yaml\nL328: \nL329:     # Enable debug logging with profiling\nL330:     glmocr parse examples/source/code.png --log-level DEBUG\nL331:     # Run layout detection on CPU (keep GPU free for OCR model)\nL332:     glmocr parse examples/source/code.png --layout-device cpu\nL333: \nL334:     # Run layout detection on a specific GPU\nL335:     glmocr parse examples/source/code.png --layout-device cuda:1\nL336: \nL337:     # Override any config value via --set (dotted path, repeatable)\nL338:     glmocr parse examples/source/code.png --set pipeline.ocr_api.api_port 8080\nL339:     glmocr parse examples/source/ --set pipeline.layout.use_polygon true --set logging.level DEBUG\nL340: #### Python API\nL341: \nL342:     from glmocr import GlmOcr, parse\nL343: \nL344:     # Simple function\nL345:     result = parse(\"image.png\")\nL346:     result = parse([\"img1.png\", \"img2.jpg\"])\nL347:     result = parse(\"https://example.com/image.png\")\nL348:     result.save(output_dir=\"./results\")\nL349: \nL350:     # Note: a list is treated as pages of a single document.\nL351: \nL352:     # Class-based API\nL353:     with GlmOcr() as parser:\nL354:         result = parser.parse(\"image.png\")\nL355:         print(result.json_result)\nL356:         result.save()\nL357:     # Place layout model on CPU (useful when GPU is reserved for OCR)\nL358:     with GlmOcr(layout_device=\"cpu\") as parser:\nL359:         result = parser.parse(\"image.png\")\nL360: \nL361:     # Place layout model on a specific GPU\nL362:     with GlmOcr(layout_device=\"cuda:1\") as parser:\nL363:         result = parser.parse(\"image.png\")\nL364: #### Flask Service\nL365: \nL366: Install the optional server dependency first:\nL367: \nL368:     pip install \"glmocr[server]\"\nL369: \nL370:     # Start service\nL371:     python -m glmocr.server\nL372: \nL373:     # With debug logging\nL374:     python -m glmocr.server --log-level DEBUG\nL375: \nL376:     # Call API\nL377:     curl -X POST http://localhost:5002/glmocr/parse \\\nL378:       -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\nL379:       -d '{\"images\": [\"./example/source/code.png\"]}'\nL380: \nL381: Semantics:\nL382:   * `images` can be a string or a list.\nL383:   * A list is treated as pages of a single document.\nL384:   * For multiple independent documents, call the endpoint multiple times (one document per request).\nL385: ### Modular Architecture\nL386: \nL387: GLM-OCR uses composable modules for easy customization:\nL388: \nL389: Component  | Description\nL390: --- | ---\nL391: `PageLoader`  | Preprocessing and image encoding\nL392: `OCRClient`  | Calls the GLM-OCR model service\nL393: `PPDocLayoutDetector`  | PP-DocLayout layout detection\nL394: `ResultFormatter`  | Post-processing, outputs JSON/Markdown\nL395: You can extend the behavior by creating custom pipelines:\nL396: \nL397:     from glmocr.dataloader import PageLoader\nL398:     from glmocr.ocr_client import OCRClient\nL399:     from glmocr.postprocess import ResultFormatter\nL400: \nL401: \nL402:     class MyPipeline:\nL403:       def __init__(self, config):\nL404:         self.page_loader = PageLoader(config)\nL405:         self.ocr_client = OCRClient(config)\nL406:         self.formatter = ResultFormatter(config)\nL407: \nL408:       def process(self, request_data):\nL409:         # Implement your own processing logic\nL410:         pass\nL411: ## Star History\nL412: \nL413: ## Acknowledgement\nL414: \nL415: This project is inspired by the excellent work of the following projects and communities:\nL416: \nL417:   * cite99†PP-DocLayout-V3†huggingface.co L418:   * cite100†PaddleOCR L419:   * cite101†MinerU L420: ## License\nL421: \nL422: The Code of this repo is under Apache License 2.0.\nL423: \nL424: The GLM-OCR model is released under the MIT License.\nL425: \nL426: The complete OCR pipeline integrates cite99†PP-DocLayoutV3†huggingface.co for document layout analysis, which is licensed under the Apache License 2.0. Users should comply with both licenses when using this project.\nL427: ## Citation\nL428: If you find GLM-OCR useful in your research, please cite our technical report:\nL429: \nL430:     @misc{duan2026glmocrtechnicalreport,\nL431:           title={GLM-OCR Technical Report},\nL432:           author={Shuaiqi Duan and Yadong Xue and Weihan Wang and Zhe Su and Huan Liu and Sheng Yang and Guobing Gan and Guo Wang and Zihan Wang and Shengdong Yan and Dexin Jin and Yuxuan Zhang and Guohong Wen and Yanfeng Wang and Yutao Zhang and Xiaohan Zhang and Wenyi Hong and Yukuo Cen and Da Yin and Bin Chen and Wenmeng Yu and Xiaotao Gu and Jie Tang},\nL433:           year={2026},\nL434:           eprint={2603.10910},\nL435:           archivePrefix={arXiv},\nL436:           primaryClass={cs.CL},\nL437:           url={https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.10910},\nL438:     }\nL439: ## About\nL440: \nL441: GLM-OCR: Accurate × Fast × Comprehensive\nL442: \nL443: ### Topics\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn25771view2 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://hunyuan.tencent.com/research\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nKimi K2.5 Tech Blog: Visual Agentic Intelligence (https://www.kimi.ai/blog/kimi-k2-5)\nciteturn25771view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.kimi.ai/blog/kimi-k2-5\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 490\n"
